+// block size, instantiated with the trip count static: two aligned 16-byte loads a block, then the same comparison order
+// as the scalar loop (a NaN wins; otherwise a greater score replaces the maximum), and a guarded scalar tail for the
+// row's last partial block. BS == 0 keeps the runtime size (every other `bsize` and every unfused-shape fallback).
